    },
    "meta": {
        "source": "figma",
        "derivableFromSource": [
            "props.type",
            "props.default",
            "layout",
            "tokens.bindings"
        ],
        "needsReview": [
            "The contract's default values (variant=soft, color=accent, size=1, highContrast=false) follow the Figma ✦ mark on variant and size. The component set's own default in Figma may be different: check defaultVariant before generating the component in code.",
            "The Figma axis is called \"highConstrast\" (typo, same as in Button). In code it is highContrast. The typo was kept in bindings.figma.property.",
            "Figma has 744 variants: 3 sizes × 4 variants × 31 colors × 2 highConstrast. All combinations exist. There are no states (hover, active, focus, disabled): the Badge is not interactive and states stays empty.",
            "The background, border and text tokens were read across all 744 variants and grouped by signature: they all follow the same pattern per color and per variant, and size does not change them. Exceptions: see the next two points.",
            "The surface background is not uniform: accent uses tokens.colors.accent-surface, neutral uses tokens.colors.surface and the other colors use step 2 of their alpha scale. That is how it is in tokens.scales.",
            "The solid text without highContrast is not uniform either: accent uses tokens.colors.accent-contrast; warning, info, sky, mint, lime, yellow and amber use tokens.colors.black-contrast; the rest, tokens.colors.white-contrast. With highContrast, the solid text always uses step 1 of the color's own scale (in Button, accent and neutral use neutral.1).",
            "The icon color (iconColor) could NOT be read: the icon is an instance and its fills are not accessible. It is assumed to be the same as the text color (usual in Radix). Verify by hand. The file's default icon is a placeholder (\"Design / inner-shadow\", 16×16).",
            "Loose values in Figma, with no variable: size 1 padding (2 / 6 px), size 3 horizontal padding (10 px), gap between icon and text for size 1 and 2 (6 px), size 1 icon size (12 px) and the border width of outline and surface (1 px, inside-aligned). 6 and 10 px do not match spacing.1, 2 or 4 (4, 8 and 16 px).",
            "One variant has an 11×12 px icon instead of 12×12 (size=1, outline, accent, highConstrast=true): it is a Figma typo, not reflected in the contract.",
            "size 1 and size 2 use the same text style (text-style.1.medium); size 3 uses text-style.2.medium. The font size in layout.fontSize (12 / 12 / 14) was inferred from the styles Link uses, not read here.",
            "Only a leading icon exists (iconStart). Unlike Button, there is no iconEnd.",
            "color has 31 values in Figma, whereas docs/components.md says \"accent, neutral, error\" for the system. The Badge is the only component with more than three colors.",
            "Product content written as a draft, not taken from Figma: description, guidance, a11y, content.label (maxLength 24), composition.forbiddenChildren and testing. My decisions: do not truncate or wrap the text (behavior.overflow), decorative icon and a maximum text length of 24 characters.",
            "Contrast not measured. The Badge has no opacity, gradients or shadows."
        ]
    }
}